@page "/tables/simple-table/column-chooser"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components.ColumnChooser
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Columns
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Filters
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Toolbar.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Localization.Resources
@using ViciOne.Ui.MonochromeIcons.Core.Enums

<h3>Column Chooser</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    The column chooser works with a <code>SimpleTable</code> the same way it does with an
    <code>AdvancedTable</code>: give the table a <code>ColumnChooserToggleId</code> and place a
    <code>ColumnChooserToggle</code> with the matching <code>Id</code> wherever the menu should appear — here
    above the table. The menu lists every chooser-eligible column; set <code>ShowInColumnChooser="false"</code>
    to keep a column always visible and out of the menu.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Hiding a column also clears any filter active on it: the header is the only place that filter can be edited,
    so keeping it would leave the data constrained by an unreachable filter. Filter the <code>Value</code>
    column below, then hide it from the menu — the rows return and re-showing the column starts filterless.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    <code>MaximumVisibleRowCount</code> limits how many columns the menu lists at once, 10 by default; any
    further ones are reached by scrolling the list, so a table with many columns cannot stretch the menu past the
    dialog or page it opens in. Here it is set to 2, one less than the columns in the menu.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="toolbar-container">
    <Toolbar>
        <ColumnChooserToggle Id="_columnChooserToggleId" MaximumVisibleRowCount="2">
            <Button>
                <ToolbarButton IconName="MonochromeIconName.ColumnChooserMenu"
                               Tooltip="@string.Format(UserActions.OpenSomething, context.PopupTitle)"
                               Active="context.PopupVisible"
                               OnClick="context.Toggle" />
            </Button>
        </ColumnChooserToggle>
    </Toolbar>
</div>

<SimpleTable Items="s_items" ColumnChooserToggleId="_columnChooserToggleId" MaximumHeight="300px">
    <Columns>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
            <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
            <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
            <FilterEditor>
                <SimpleTableContainsColumnFilterEditor ValueSelector="x => x.Value" />
            </FilterEditor>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp">
            <CellContent>@context.Timestamp</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Id" Title="Id" ShowInColumnChooser="false">
            <CellContent>@context.Id</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
    </Columns>
</SimpleTable>
